  "slug": "instant-pot-black-beans",
  "name": "Instant Pot Black Beans",
  "recipe_type": "side",
  "brief_description": "Using an Instant Pot to cook black beans is an easy, speedy alternative to soaking and boiling dried beans.",
  "cuisine": "American Latin Caribbean",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Pour beans into a multi-functional pressure cooker (such as Instant Pot). Cover with a few inches of cool water. Close and lock the lid. Select Manual; set timer for 21 minutes on high pressure according to manufacturer's instructions. Allow 10 to 15 minutes for pressure to build."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Release pressure using the natural-release method according to manufacturer's instructions, 10 to 40 minutes. Unlock and remove the lid. Drain beans and let cool."
    }
  ],
